{"id": "6214e7e9acb29630abbb5405", "name": "Chinese Hackers Target Taiwan's Financial Trading Sector with Supply Chain Attack", "description": "An advanced persistent threat (APT) group operating with objectives aligned with the Chinese government has been linked to an organized supply chain attack on Taiwan's financial sector. The attacks are said to have first commenced at the end of November 2021, with the intrusions attributed to a threat actor tracked as APT10, also known as Stone Panda, the MenuPass group, and Bronze Riverside, and known to be active since at least 2009.\n\nThe second wave of attacks hit a peak between February 10 and 13, 2022, according to a new report published by Taiwanese cybersecurity firm CyCraft, which said the wide-ranging supply chain compromise specifically targeted the software systems of financial institutions, resulting in \"abnormal cases of placing orders.\"", "author_name": "dekaRituraj", "modified": "2022-03-24T00:00:00.271000", "created": "2022-02-22T13:40:57.485000", "tags": ["dotnet", "webshell", "quasar rat", "sharpsploit", "operation cache panda"], "references": ["https://medium.com/cycraft/supply-chain-attack-targeting-taiwan-financial-sector-bae2f0962934", "https://thehackernews.com/2022/02/chinese-hackers-target-taiwans.html"], "public": 1, "adversary": "", "targeted_countries": ["Taiwan"], "malware_families": ["QuasarRAT - S0262"], "attack_ids": ["T1569.002", "T1543.003", "T1047", "T1021.001", "T1505.003", "T1082", "T1518.001", "T1543.003", "T1055", "T1027", "T1480", "T1562.001"], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "indicators": [{"id": 3382091119, "indicator": "03b88fd80414edeabaaa6bb55d1d09fc", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2022-02-22T13:40:57", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 3382091120, "indicator": "0724ac34e997354ca9fb06d57af4e29b", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2022-02-22T13:40:57", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration":